ull,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.16175835767012603,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.07150085353907763,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.042969998,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":28.6,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Affirm Holdings, Inc. operates payment network in the United States, Canada, and internationally. Its platform offers pay-over-time solutions at checkout for both consumers and merchants. The company's commerce platform, agreements with originating banks, and capital markets partners enables consumers to pay for a purchase over time. It has active merchants covering small businesses, large enterprises, direct-to-consumer brands, brick-and-mortar stores, and companies with an omni-channel presence. The company's merchants represent a range of industries, including electronics; equipment and auto; fashion and beauty; general merchandise; home and lifestyle services; sporting goods and outdoors; and travel and ticketing. Affirm Holdings, Inc. was founded in 2012 and is headquartered in San Francisco, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Max Roth Levchin | Founder, CEO & Chairman | Age 49 | Compensation: $552,145 (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $1.8M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 37%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $421K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $129K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Affirm Holdings, Inc. is a large-cap financial services business with a $23.0B market cap on $4.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +39% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +10.7pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -24% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $993M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 23 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders. Cash conversion is thin at 0.64\u00d7, however, which raises the oldest question in analysis: are these earnings backed by cash?.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 11.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 4.3% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 77% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7734365701845112},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Financial Services peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 19% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $23.9M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Stock Analysts\u2019 Ratings Reiterations for November 6th (ABNB, ACLS, AFRM, ALB, ARLO, ATO, AUTO, AXON, BETA, BTA)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/stock-analysts-ratings-reiterations-for-november-6th-abnb-acls-afrm-alb-arlo-ato-auto-axon-beta-bta.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793990688.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Affirm Holdings (AFRM) Faces A 29% Fair Value Gap As Earnings Land","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/affirm-holdings-afrm-faces-29-181307150.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793988787.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.55,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title